 {R}←∆DQ names;⎕TRAP;caller;class;type;HR;timers;event;done;interrupt;tkn;m;i;types;z;modal;ID;conn;e;n;id;obs;pre;TIMERNAME;TIMERACTIVE;timer;OLDTIMER;level;tid
 ⎕TRAP←0 'S'

 caller←findCaller

 ⍝ Nesting depth, counted explicitly rather than read off ⎕SI.
 ⍝
 ⍝ It used to be `1⌈+/⎕SI∊⊂'∆DQ'`, which cannot see the outer ⎕DQ at all:
 ⍝ callbacks are dispatched through execUserCode's 86⌶, so a modal opened from
 ⍝ a callback has a stack like
 ⍝     ∆DQ QUESTION REDEAL SETUP ...
 ⍝ with no trace of the ∆DQ that dispatched it. The nested call therefore
 ⍝ computed level 1 and reused TIMER1 -- the very object the outer ⎕DQ was
 ⍝ waiting on. Answering the modal satisfied BOTH: the outer ⎕DQ returned, its
 ⍝ caller ran to completion, and the application was left drawn on screen but
 ⍝ dead, ignoring every event. Opening a modal from a callback is one of the
 ⍝ most common ⎕WC patterns there is, so this is not a corner.
 ⍝
 ⍝ Depth is per thread: separate threads run independent ⎕DQs and must not
 ⍝ share a queue.
 tid←⎕TID
 :If 2≠caller._EWC.⎕NC'DQTIDS'
     caller._EWC.(DQTIDS DQDEPTHS)←⍬ ⍬
 :EndIf
 i←caller._EWC.DQTIDS⍳tid
 :If i>≢caller._EWC.DQTIDS
     caller._EWC.DQTIDS,←tid
     caller._EWC.DQDEPTHS,←0
 :EndIf
 level←caller._EWC.DQDEPTHS[i]←1+i⊃caller._EWC.DQDEPTHS
 TIMERNAME←'TIMER',⍕level ⍝ A queue of its own for each nesting level
 OLDTIMER←caller._EWC.TIMERACTIVE

 names←,⊆names
 names←⊃¨caller removeCaller¨names
 modal←0

 :If ~∧/(∊names)∊'.#'  ⍝ '.' (all) / '#' (root) DQ tokens; ∊ normalises depth — ⊃¨removeCaller leaves them nested, so a bare names∊'.' '#' spuriously fails
     ⎕SIGNAL(∨/~(caller.⎕NC z←names,¨⊂'.Type')∊2.1 ¯2.6)/11
     types←,⊆caller⍎⍕z
     :If modal←∧/types∊modalClasses
         'Only one modal object at a time'⎕SIGNAL(1≠≢names)/11
         R←,⊆dWX(⊃names)'OnlyDQ'(⊃names)
         :If (1↑⊃R)≢1↑names ⍝ Validate echo-back
             'E' Log 'Internal error: OnlyDQD returned an unexpected result: ',,⍕R
             'INTERNAL ERROR' ⎕SIGNAL 11
         :EndIf
         :If USEHR
             ((⊃names),'.HR')caller.⎕WS('Visible' 1)('Size'(HRBorder+1↓⊃R))
         :EndIf

     :EndIf
     :If ∨/m←types∊nativeClasses ⍝ TCPSocket or other things(?)
         'May not mix DQ of native and EWC classes'⎕SIGNAL(0∊m)/11
         →0⊣R←caller.⎕DQ names
     :EndIf
 :EndIf

 obs←,⊂(pre←(⍕caller),'.'),'_EWC.',TIMERNAME ⍝ The object which implements our message queue
 :If 9≠⎕NC ⊃obs ⍝ If it was not created in make_EWC
 :OrIf ⎕TID≠(⍎⊃obs).TID
     timer←make_EWC_TIMER caller._EWC
 :EndIf

 caller._EWC.TIMERACTIVE←TIMERNAME
 (⊃obs) ⎕WS 'Data' names
 :If USEHR ⍝ In Desktop mode, also DQ all the HTMLRenderers
     obs,←pre∘,¨names,¨(modal∨types∊⊂'Form')/¨⊂'.HR'
 :EndIf

 done←interrupt←0
 (ID conn)←getConnection caller(⊃names)

 :Trap 1002 1003 ⍝ Catch interrupts
     ⎕←'∆DQ in thread ',(⍕⎕TID),' ⎕DQing ',⍕names
     z←⎕DQ obs        ⍝ Should only exit on 1002 to TIMER
     R←3⊃z
     ⎕←'DQ of ' obs 'returned' z
 :Else
     interrupt←1 ⋄ R←⍬
 :EndTrap

 :If 0≠≢R
     z←⊢/R
     :If 9=⎕NC'z.Event'
         ⍝ eventNumber for the same reason processEvent uses it: ⎕WC reports
         ⍝ events numerically, and ⎕DQ's result is the other route back into
         ⍝ user code. `R←61=2⊃⎕DQ'QUESTION_MSGBOX'` -- the standard way to ask
         ⍝ which button a Query box got -- compares against a character vector
         ⍝ otherwise, yielding a boolean vector and a RANK ERROR in the caller.
         R←z.Event.((ID(#.EWC.eventNumber EventName)),{6::⍵ ⋄ Info}⍬) ⍝ /// Need a proper queue
     :Else
         ∘∘∘
     :EndIf ⍝ Else return R as is
 :EndIf

 :If modal ⍝ Exit from Modal mode
     :If USEHR
         ((⊃names),'.HR')caller.⎕WS'Visible' 0
     :EndIf
     z←dWX(⊃names)'OnlyDQ'
 :EndIf
 'INTERRUPT'⎕SIGNAL interrupt/999

 caller._EWC.TIMERACTIVE←OLDTIMER
 caller._EWC.DQDEPTHS[i]←level-1
 :If level>1 ⍝ More that one level of DQ
     ⎕EX ⊃obs
 :EndIf
